From 6331558ca87b02d6019a09c4a733317e1dfb2911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:49:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v2 2/9] sparc32: flush the source user alias in
 copy_user_highpage()

copy_user_highpage() also handles lowmem pages. A source user alias can be
dirtied after the fork cache flush but before write protection and its TLB
shootdown complete on another CPU. This explains why flushing at fork
alone is insufficient; the historical tests below did not isolate that
particular interleaving.

The hyperSPARC external cache is virtually indexed, so index bits lie
above the page offset and one physical page can occupy 64, 128 or 256
distinct cache locations depending on cache size. Two mappings of a page
do not see each other's dirty lines.

copy_user_highpage() reads the source through a kmap_local alias, so lines
dirtied through the user mapping sit in a different set and the copy reads
stale memory. copy_user_page() then flushes page_address(page), NULL for a
highmem page, with no NULL check.

Flush the source page's user alias with flush_cache_page() before reading
it, and flush the destination through the address actually written.

For lowmem, kmap_local_page() returns the direct mapping and kunmap_local()
does not invoke the kmap cache hooks. A previous kernel read can therefore
leave clean supervisor cache lines at the source's kernel address. After
the surviving process reuses and modifies the page through a different
user alias, flushing that user alias alone does not remove those lines.

Flush the source kernel alias immediately before copy_page(), after the
user alias flush, to discard stale source lines. Flush it again after the
copy to retire the clean lines just loaded before later user writes.
Keep both flushes explicit for lowmem and highmem; correctness must not
depend on the kmap hooks introduced later in this series.

Only observable on HyperSPARC: SuperSPARC's caches are physically indexed
and MBus snooped, so viking_flush_cache_all() is a window flush and a
return.

Historical fork/COW torture on a two-cpu SPARCstation 20: 7 of 20 runs
lost writes before the user-alias fix, 0 of 20 after. These results predate
the source kernel-alias flushes and do not validate the new reuse case.

The source-alias omission predates Git history; the later folio conversion
also removed sparc_flush_page_to_ram()'s NULL guard. This change uses the
mapped destination address and covers both cases.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/include/asm/page_32.h |  6 ++++++
 arch/sparc/mm/init_32.c          | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/include/asm/page_32.h b/arch/sparc/include/asm/page_32.h
index 7429291fb118..c968ec33ee98 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/include/asm/page_32.h
+++ b/arch/sparc/include/asm/page_32.h
@@ -28,6 +28,12 @@
 		(void)(vaddr);			\
 	} while (0)
 
+#define __HAVE_ARCH_COPY_USER_HIGHPAGE
+struct page;
+struct vm_area_struct;
+void copy_user_highpage(struct page *to, struct page *from,
+			unsigned long vaddr, struct vm_area_struct *vma);
+
 /* passing structs on the Sparc slow us down tremendously... */
 
 /* #define STRICT_MM_TYPECHECKS */
diff --git a/arch/sparc/mm/init_32.c b/arch/sparc/mm/init_32.c
index 2f693b70dbd8..00bcaebb108a 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/mm/init_32.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/mm/init_32.c
@@ -103,6 +103,31 @@ void sparc_flush_page_to_ram(struct page *page)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(sparc_flush_page_to_ram);
 
+/*
+ * Write back the source user alias before copying through the kernel alias.
+ * Lowmem kmap_local mappings bypass the cache hooks, so explicitly flush
+ * the source kernel alias both before reading and after filling it. This
+ * avoids stale reads and leaves no source alias behind for later user writes.
+ * Flush the destination through its mapped address, also valid for highmem.
+ */
+void copy_user_highpage(struct page *to, struct page *from,
+			unsigned long vaddr, struct vm_area_struct *vma)
+{
+	char *vfrom, *vto;
+
+	if (vma)
+		flush_cache_page(vma, vaddr, page_to_pfn(from));
+
+	vfrom = kmap_local_page(from);
+	vto = kmap_local_page(to);
+	__flush_page_to_ram((unsigned long)vfrom);
+	copy_page(vto, vfrom);
+	__flush_page_to_ram((unsigned long)vfrom);
+	__flush_page_to_ram((unsigned long)vto);
+	kunmap_local(vto);
+	kunmap_local(vfrom);
+}
+
 void sparc_flush_folio_to_ram(struct folio *folio)
 {
 	unsigned long vaddr = (unsigned long)folio_address(folio);
-- 
